#
# The merge source under `R` is itself a mapping that merges: its own `<<` brings the integer `1`
# and then the string `"1"`, a collision inside the source, with the integer's value `a` standing.
# The enclosing merge then takes the source apart and copies its one entry into `R`, so the source
# is never walked as a mapping of its own; the notice follows the entry into `R` and is printed at
# /R/1 ("first at L:3,C:12 and again at L:3,C:22. The first value is the one evaluated."). One notice.
#
rule the_held_value_stands_under_r { R."1" == "a" }
